// The entry of the two-module program `zen build src/pair` compiles.
//
// It names a type and a function declared in the OTHER file and uses
// both, so it does not check unless the two modules' nodes are in one
// `Ast`: a `Checker` is built from one tree and every question it
// answers is about an id, and an id from a tree it does not hold means
// nothing.
//
// It also DECLARES a type the other file names, which is what makes
// neither module stand alone: drop either one from the tree and the
// other references an id that is not in it.

Leaf, leaf_value = pair

Tag* = {
    mark*: i32,
}

twice* = () i32 { leaf_value() + leaf_value() }

boxed* = () Leaf { Leaf(n: twice()) }
